<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · Protest and freedom · 1908 · Europe</p><h1 class="sg-title">Bandiera Rossa</h1><p class="sg-kid" data-say>An Italian workers' song of 1908 in praise of the red flag, the sign of the socialist and communist movements.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Carlo Tuzzi</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>traditional (the melody is taken from two Lombard folk songs)</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>the Italian labour movement; socialist and communist parties</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Italy (the melody from Lombardy)</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>1908</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem · Protest and freedom</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (lyrics by Carlo Tuzzi, written 1908; melody from two Lombard folk songs)</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandiera-rossa">Bandiera Rossa</a>&quot; (&quot;Red Flag&quot;) is one of the best-known songs of the Italian labour movement. It celebrates the red flag as the symbol of the socialist and communist movements. Carlo Tuzzi wrote the text in 1908 and set it to a melody taken from two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> folk songs. The song is often called by its opening words instead, partly to avoid confusion with &quot;Le tre bandiere&quot;, another Italian socialist song.</p><p>The text did not stay fixed. Several variants came to be identified with particular socialist or communist parties. After the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a>, two closing lines in praise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a> and liberty were added and the opening line was changed; in more recent renderings the word for communism at the end of the chorus is often replaced by the word for socialism.</p><p>The song has been sung in many languages, among them English, Serbo-Croatian, Slovenian, German, French, Swedish, Turkish, Kurdish, Finnish, Maltese, Russian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esperanto">Esperanto</a>, Indonesian, Japanese, Arabic, Hindi, Punjabi, Vietnamese and Filipino. Composers and performers have returned to it: Frederic Rzewski quoted it in two piano works of the 1970s, punk bands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> recorded it from the 1980s, and the 1986 Israeli film named after its opening words shows Israeli and Egyptian soldiers singing it mockingly in the Sinai after the 1967 War.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A song in praise of the red flag as the emblem of the workers' cause. It calls working people forward to struggle and ends in a cheer for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a> (or, in later versions, socialism) and liberty. Its mood is rousing and confident.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">Italian</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-2"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Italian</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Avanti popolo, alla riscossa</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Forward, people, to the fight back,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa, bandiera rossa;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>red flag, red flag;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">avanti popolo, alla riscossa</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>forward, people, to the fight back,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa trionferà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag will triumph.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Avanti popolo, tuona il cannone</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Forward, people, the cannon thunders,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione, rivoluzione</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution, revolution,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">avanti popolo, tuona il cannone</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>forward, people, the cannon thunders,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione vogliamo far.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Rivoluzione noi vogliamo far</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom.</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 48 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Bandiera rossa dove sei stata</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Red flag, where have you been?</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">sei ritornata, sei ritornata</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>you have come back, you have come back,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa dove sei stata</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>red flag, where have you been?</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">sei ritornata a sventolar.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>you have come back to wave.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Rivoluzione noi vogliamo far</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Sei ritornata con il tuo martello</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>You have come back with your hammer,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">falce e martello falce e martello</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>sickle and hammer, sickle and hammer,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">sei ritornata con il tuo martello</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>you have come back with your hammer,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">falce e martello trionferà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>sickle and hammer will triumph.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Rivoluzione noi vogliamo far</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Dai campi al mare alle miniere</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>From the fields to the sea, to the mines,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rosse bandiere rosse bandiere</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>red flags, red flags,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">dai campi al mare alle miniere</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from the fields to the sea, to the mines,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rosse bandiere sventoleran.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>red flags will wave.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Rivoluzione noi vogliamo far</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">rivoluzione noi vogliamo far;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>revolution is what we want to make;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Non più nemici non più frontiere</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>No more enemies, no more frontiers:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">sono i confini rosse bandiere</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the borders are red flags,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">o proletari alla riscossa</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>O proletarians, to the fight back,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa trionferà.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag will triumph.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">Bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">bandiera rossa la trionferà</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the red flag, it will triumph,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="it">evviva il comunismo e la libertà!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>long live communism and freedom!</span></p></div></details></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Anonymous; first words by Carlo Tuzzi (1908). Text from <a href="https://it.wikisource.org/wiki/Bandiera_rossa_(Avanti_popolo%2C_tuona_il_cannone)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p><p>The English is the Institute&#8217;s own translation, made from the original for this page.</p></div><details class="sg-notes"><summary>Notes on the translation (5)</summary><ul><li>line 1.1: 'alla riscossa' = to the counter-attack, to rise up and win back what was lost.</li><li>line 2.1: 'la trionferà': 'la' is the popular, northern Italian subject pronoun ('it'), repeating 'bandiera rossa'.</li><li>line 3.4: 'rivoluzione vogliamo far' = literally 'revolution we want to make'.</li><li>line 11.2: 'sono i confini rosse bandiere' = the borders are red flags (the only borders left are the red flags).</li><li>source: the imported original has the stanza line numbers (4, 8, 12 … 48) run into the last line of each stanza ('4bandiera rossa', ' 8 evviva'); they are not translated. The import should drop them (nonum or a text fix).</li></ul></details></section>
